Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||08-31-2001||12:48 PM||||Doug is active on the Fiero racing list which I moderate.<P>Scott backer..haven't heard that name in about 2 years. He lives in Upstate NY , I believe in law enforcement. If you ever needed a part # he had it.<P>I was on the Peter Z. List for the first time 6 years ago.<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000003||TopFiero||08-31-2001||02:20 PM||||  That's good to hear that Doug's still around.  Probably still doing well racing that '88 Formula of his.  Someone should invite him over to this board, it'd be great to talk to him on a forum like this instead of a mailing list.  He had a friend that usually raced a Ford Probe, but occasionally joined him in SCCA C class competition driving the Fiero, as I recall he always took first place, even in a car he wasn't all that familiar with... beating out many of the cars in A and B class.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||08-31-2001||06:42 PM||||I still am on the lists, but I don't post much. More fun on here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||banditbalz||08-31-2001||07:24 PM||||Anybody ever hear from George Ryan? He has/had a 1900lb quad 4 powered notchback that used to race in SCCA events...<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||09-01-2001||07:46 PM||||George had a mild heart attack last week , but is back on the net and doing fine. He is haveing a 4.9ltr Caddy powered 86 SE built for the street , the quad 4 car has been sold to Greg duncan who autocrosses a 4.9ltr 85 GT.<P>George is Currently building a car for the GRM $2002 Challenge. a 4.9ltr 88 coupe.<P>basically you autocross and drag race the car in the challenge , but the cars cost can't exceed $2002 , best combined score , wins.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Doug Chase||09-04-2001||12:49 PM||||Hi TopFiero,<P>I'm still around.  Somebody pointed me to this topic so I registered and replied.  I'm still on the Fiero.org list and post occasionally.  I'm more active on the racing list.  <P>I haven't been autocrossing much in the past couple years because I've sort of moved on to a new form of racing -- rally!  Over the past couple years I've been building an '85 GT into a rally car.  I finished in in March and have done two events so far.  My next one is this weekend.  I have a couple action shots of the car that I can post if somebody wants to tell me how.  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Doug Chase<BR>Duvall, WA<BR>'88 Fiero Formula 5-spd (autocrosser)<BR>'88 Fiero GT 5-spd (daily driver)<BR>'85 Fiero GT 4-spd (rally car)||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||09-04-2001||11:08 PM||||Hi Doug, welcome to the fourm!<P>I know we'd all love to hear more about your rally car, that sounds like too much fun on 4 wheels to be legal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  How does it drive? what have you done to it? Can it do my laundry?!<P>If you want just email me the pics, I'd love to see them!!!<P><BR>(to post them, first you need to upload them to a webserver, then make a 'link' or tag in your post to them.  There is a piece of software for windows called "PIP" or "Pennock's Image Poster" that will take care of the webserver end, it's for windows computers.)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Doug Chase:<BR><B>Hi TopFiero,<P>I'm still around.  Somebody pointed me to this topic so I registered and replied.  I'm still on the Fiero.org list and post occasionally.  I'm more active on the racing list.  <P>I haven't been autocrossing much in the past couple years because I've sort of moved on to a new form of racing -- rally!  Over the past couple years I've been building an '85 GT into a rally car.  I finished in in March and have done two events so far.  My next one is this weekend.  I have a couple action shots of the car that I can post if somebody wants to tell me how.  <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000009||TopFiero||09-06-2001||11:49 AM||||  Hi Doug!  I just saw your post.  It's sure been a while.  Glad to hear you're still racing, rally has got to be a wild experience.  To post a pic, use {img}url{/img} and replace the curved brackets with straight brackets.  If it doesn't take, you can always edit the message later to adjust.<P>  How does the Fiero do in rally and do they use a class structure similar to SCCA?  I'd be interested to know what kind of cars you compete against.<P>  I think our local club has kind of fizzled, so finding fellow owners to race these days is getting tricky.  We used to have 4 or 5 Fieros show up on regular Sunday autocrosses.  I haven't seen or heard from Paul in about two years and his website hasn't been updated since August of 2000.  Hopefully SWIFC still exists, a few of the members enjoyed racing.  I wanted to get back into racing now that my Fiero is a 3rd car.  I'm going to work on the car over the winter (GT conversion, suspension improvements, engine work, etc), and I'll try to start racing next spring.  Should be fun!||||reg||1
