Z||000014||Kelvin Vivian||01-01-2002||05:01 AM||||Hey TopFiero,<P>There were some good times on that ol' Fiero email list.  One person on that list convinced me to buy the 88 GT T-Top that I have now (pictured below), I just about passed it up as I didn't know how rare this particular model was at the time (and still is).  Visit <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org," TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.org,</A>  one of the "original" Fiero sites,  and click on the <B>who's who</B> link and you will see most of those who were on that list (I wonder who's on that list that is also here on this forum... I posted there back in 1993 or 94 when I had my first Fiero, a 1985 SE 4-cyl 5-spd...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>On another reminiscent note, Peter Zurich created the first Fiero site that I ever visited on the www.  That was back around 1992-93 when the www was just about new... Seeing info on the net about the Fiero was awesome, I still remember that pic of the red 85 GT that he had on the first page, I enjoyed visiting that site as I enjoy visiting this site. Good stuff Pennock.<P>KV<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=3&courtesy=1">     <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
